  "step_3": "The decision reason relies on assessing the skewness of the outcome distribution, particularly the concentration of probability on favorable (less negative) outcomes, and prefers the more left-skewed lottery (Lottery B in this case). However, the individual’s deliberation focuses on computing expected values, as indicated by the verbal report. The individual does not mention or imply any focus on the shape of the distribution, such as concentration of probability on better outcomes or skewness. Instead, the reasoning is explicitly aligned with expected value calculation. Although both approaches may sometimes align, here the individual’s stated rule (expected value) differs from the skewness-based rule. There is no evidence in the verbal report that the individual assessed how probabilities are distributed across favorable vs. unfavorable outcomes in a way that reflects skewness evaluation. Therefore, the decision reason based on skewness was not used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
}

